# GitHub Commit Standards

This document outlines the standards for making commits to the BrogueMCP GitHub repository, with special focus on the BrogueMCP module.

## Commit Message Format

All commit messages should follow this format:

```
[Module] Short summary (under 50 chars)

More detailed explanatory text, if necessary. Wrap it to about 72 characters.
Explain what the commit does, why it was made, and any relevant context.

- Bullet points are acceptable
- Typically hyphen or asterisk is used for the bullet

If applicable, reference related issues or pull requests:
Fixes #123, Relates to #456
```

## Module Prefixes

Use one of these module prefixes at the start of your commit message:

- `[BrogueMCP]` - Changes to the BrogueMCP module
- `[DM-Agent]` - Changes to the Dungeon Master AI agent
- `[UI]` - Changes to user interface components
- `[Engine]` - Changes to the game engine
- `[Doc]` - Documentation changes
- `[Test]` - Test-related changes
- `[Infra]` - Infrastructure or build system changes

## Branch Strategy

### Main Branches
- `main` - Production-ready code
- `development` - Active development branch

### Feature Branches
Feature branches should follow the naming convention:
```
feature/short-descriptive-name
```

### Fix Branches
Fix branches should follow the naming convention:
```
fix/issue-number-short-description
```

## Commit Guidelines

1. **Atomic Commits** - Each commit should represent a single logical change
2. **Complete Commits** - The codebase should build/work after each commit
3. **Clear Messages** - Commit messages should clearly explain what changed and why
4. **Reference Issues** - Link commits to GitHub issues when applicable

## Automated Quality Checks

The following checks will be automatically performed on commits:

- Code style compliance
- Build verification
- Test suite execution
- Documentation standards
- Memory leak detection (for C code)

## Examples

Good commit message:
```
[BrogueMCP] Add narrator personality system

Implements a configurable narrator personality system for the Dungeon Master AI:
- Adds personality attributes and presets
- Creates UI for adjusting narrator voice
- Integrates with prompt generation system

The system allows players to customize the storytelling style during gameplay.
Fixes #789
```

Bad commit message:
```
fixed stuff
```

## Using This Rule

The Cursor editor will prompt you to format your commit messages according to these standards. When committing, ensure you:

1. Include the appropriate module prefix
2. Write a clear, concise summary line
3. Add detailed explanation as needed
4. Reference related issues

## Automation with Cursor

When using the Cursor editor, you can:

1. Use the command palette and search for "Commit with Conventional Format"
2. The editor will prompt you for the module and summary
3. A properly formatted commit message will be generated
4. You can then add details as needed 